        <li><a href="#install"><span class="stop">S1</span>Install the line</a></li>
        <li><a href="#connect"><span class="stop">S2</span>Connect and drive</a></li>
        <li><a href="#serialize"><span class="stop">S3</span>Serialized access</a></li>
        <li><a href="#configure"><span class="stop">S4</span>Configure and export</a></li>
        <li><a href="#encrypt"><span class="stop">S5</span>Encrypted databases</a></li>
        <li><a href="#limits"><span class="stop">S6</span>Platform limits</a></li>
        <li><a href="#skills"><span class="stop">S7</span>Agent skills</a></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="prose">
        <section class="block" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-h">
          <h2 id="install-h">Install the line</h2>
          <p>
            One dependency on top of <code class="inline">package:sqlite3</code>. One instance serves both packages, so import one of the two clashing <code class="inline">Table</code>/<code class="inline">Column</code> definitions with a prefix:
          </p>
